    {
      "id": "M0W-NrYpfTOdgN13wAGFH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7460.172145394363,
      "y": -1200.1766183708464,
      "width": 1776.3477783203125,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 887035170,
      "version": 155,
      "versionNonce": 346798114,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786289205373,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A new patient_id is always minted first (f\"P-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}\").\nThe code doesn't look up whether the patient already exists before inserting.\n\nIt just attempts the INSERT and lets Postgres enforce the rule.\n\nIf idx_patients_identity rejects it (same lower(last_name), lower(first_name), dob already present), \npsycopg2 raises errors.UniqueViolation, which is caught at:",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A new patient_id is always minted first (f\"P-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}\").\nThe code doesn't look up whether the patient already exists before inserting.\n\nIt just attempts the INSERT and lets Postgres enforce the rule.\n\nIf idx_patients_identity rejects it (same lower(last_name), lower(first_name), dob already present), \npsycopg2 raises errors.UniqueViolation, which is caught at:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
