      "text": "| Model                                                                                       | Latency / Quality                                                     | Cost (~per minute)                                                                                                    | Notable Limits                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **OpenAI GPT-Realtime-2.1**                                                                 | Fastest (~320ms), strongest reasoning                                 | ~$0.24–0.30/min (audio output alone is $64/M tokens) — meaningfully pricier than either Nova                          | Locked to OpenAI's own voices (9 choices); no swapping to Claude/Gemini/open models    |\n| **Google Gemini Live API**                                                                  | Strong, and by far the widest language coverage (97 languages)        | “Orders of magnitude cheaper” than GPT-Realtime per the comparison sources                                            | Less telephony-specific tuning called out than either Nova                             |\n| **Amazon Nova Sonic** (original, `amazon.nova-sonic-v1:0` — currently used by this project) | Good, telephony-tuned; launched March 2025                            | ~$3/M input, $12/M output speech tokens — roughly **~$0.015/min**                                                     | Only 5 languages: English, Spanish, French, Italian, German                            |\n| **Amazon Nova 2 Sonic** (`amazon.nova-2-sonic-v1:0`)                                        | Same telephony tuning, plus improved turn-taking/tool-calling per AWS | Same ballpark pricing as original (**~$0.015/min**) — AWS public pricing doesn't clearly separate the two generations | 7 languages (adds Portuguese, Hindi); only 3 regions so far; newer, less battle-tested |\n| **xAI Grok Voice**                                                                          | Described as “a strong challenger”                                    | **$0.05/min** flat                                                                                                    | Less documented, smaller ecosystem                                                     |\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| Model                                                                                       | Latency / Quality                                                     | Cost (~per minute)                                                                                                    | Notable Limits                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **OpenAI GPT-Realtime-2.1**                                                                 | Fastest (~320ms), strongest reasoning                                 | ~$0.24–0.30/min (audio output alone is $64/M tokens) — meaningfully pricier than either Nova                          | Locked to OpenAI's own voices (9 choices); no swapping to Claude/Gemini/open models    |\n| **Google Gemini Live API**                                                                  | Strong, and by far the widest language coverage (97 languages)        | “Orders of magnitude cheaper” than GPT-Realtime per the comparison sources                                            | Less telephony-specific tuning called out than either Nova                             |\n| **Amazon Nova Sonic** (original, `amazon.nova-sonic-v1:0` — currently used by this project) | Good, telephony-tuned; launched March 2025                            | ~$3/M input, $12/M output speech tokens — roughly **~$0.015/min**                                                     | Only 5 languages: English, Spanish, French, Italian, German                            |\n| **Amazon Nova 2 Sonic** (`amazon.nova-2-sonic-v1:0`)                                        | Same telephony tuning, plus improved turn-taking/tool-calling per AWS | Same ballpark pricing as original (**~$0.015/min**) — AWS public pricing doesn't clearly separate the two generations | 7 languages (adds Portuguese, Hindi); only 3 regions so far; newer, less battle-tested |\n| **xAI Grok Voice**                                                                          | Described as “a strong challenger”                                    | **$0.05/min** flat                                                                                                    | Less documented, smaller ecosystem                                                     |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
