      "text": "1. Tell the two background workers to stop.\n\n2. Send Bedrock the \"we're ending the session\" messages.\n\n3. Close the mail slot so nothing more can be sent.\n\n4. Wait for the reply-listening worker to actually notice the session ended and finish its loop — \nthat's the await response_task step. \nIt's just \"don't walk away until that worker has finished cleaning up,\" \nwith a 2-second patience limit before forcing it to stop.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Tell the two background workers to stop.\n\n2. Send Bedrock the \"we're ending the session\" messages.\n\n3. Close the mail slot so nothing more can be sent.\n\n4. Wait for the reply-listening worker to actually notice the session ended and finish its loop — \nthat's the await response_task step. \nIt's just \"don't walk away until that worker has finished cleaning up,\" \nwith a 2-second patience limit before forcing it to stop.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "o-9bNmF3IgKzmrRXCLhSd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 37924.92004130709,
      "y": -1069.2725658191396,
      "width": 1462.9998779296875,
      "height": 2485,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bRW",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 788246027,
      "version": 98,
      "versionNonce": 747011909,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787681109854,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "========================== test_bedrock_stream.py ==========================\n                    (manual smoke-test script -- not pytest)\n\n  generate_tone_pcm16()          load_wav_pcm16(path)            stub_tool_executor(name, args)\n   builds 2s/440Hz sine wave      opens a real .wav,               always returns\n   as raw PCM16 bytes             validates 16kHz/mono/16bit,      {\"error\": \"tool dispatch not\n   [fallback if no arg given]     strips header, returns            wired up yet\"}\n        |                         raw PCM16 frames                       |\n        |                         [used when a path IS given]            | passed in as\n        |                              |                                 |\n        +-------------+----------------+                                 |\n                       | picked by                                       |\n                       v                                                 v\n                     main()  ----------------------------------------> BedrockStreamManager(\n                       |                                                  tool_executor=...)\n                       v\n  sys.argv[1] given? --yes--> audio = load_wav_pcm16(wav_path)\n        |no                        (raises w/ ffmpeg fix-it command\n        v                           if format doesn't match)\n  audio = generate_tone_pcm16()\n        |\n        v\n  await manager.initialize_stream()\n        |   (opens REAL bidirectional connection to AWS Bedrock,\n        |    spawns _process_responses() + _process_audio_input())\n        v\n  await manager.send_audio_content_start_event()\n        |   (\"AUDIO content block starting\" -> sent to Bedrock)\n        v\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  chunked send loop  [NEW -- replaces single add_audio_chunk] |\n  |--------------------------------------------------------------|\n  |  chunk_bytes = 100ms worth of 16kHz/16-bit/mono audio        |\n  |  for each 100ms slice of `audio`:                            |\n  |     manager.add_audio_chunk(slice)                           |\n  |        (drops onto audio_input_queue; background loop #1     |\n  |         ships it via send_raw_event() -- same as before)     |\n  |     await asyncio.sleep(0.1)                                 |\n  |        (paces it like a live mic feed instead of one blob)   |\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  await asyncio.sleep(0.5)\n        |   (give the last chunk a moment to actually go out)\n        v\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  event-watch loop   [while True, timeout=8.0]                |\n  |---------------------------------------------------------------\n  |   event = await manager.output_queue.get()                   |\n  |   print(f\"EVENT: {keys}\")                                    |\n  |   \"completionEnd\" in event?  --yes--> break                  |\n  |   8s pass with nothing new?  --------> TimeoutError -> break |\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  drain manager.audio_output_queue --> audio_out bytearray\n        v\n  await manager.close()\n        |   (cancels pending tool tasks + audio_input_task,\n        |    sends audio-end / prompt-end / session-end events,\n        |    closes input_stream, awaits response_task)\n        v\n  +-----------------------------+        +--------------------------------+\n  |  audio_out non-empty?       | yes -->|  write bedrock_test_output.wav |\n  +-----------------------------+        +--------------------------------+\n        | no\n        v\n  print(\"No audio received back.\")\n\nEntry point:  if __name__ == \"__main__\": asyncio.run(main())\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "========================== test_bedrock_stream.py ==========================\n                    (manual smoke-test script -- not pytest)\n\n  generate_tone_pcm16()          load_wav_pcm16(path)            stub_tool_executor(name, args)\n   builds 2s/440Hz sine wave      opens a real .wav,               always returns\n   as raw PCM16 bytes             validates 16kHz/mono/16bit,      {\"error\": \"tool dispatch not\n   [fallback if no arg given]     strips header, returns            wired up yet\"}\n        |                         raw PCM16 frames                       |\n        |                         [used when a path IS given]            | passed in as\n        |                              |                                 |\n        +-------------+----------------+                                 |\n                       | picked by                                       |\n                       v                                                 v\n                     main()  ----------------------------------------> BedrockStreamManager(\n                       |                                                  tool_executor=...)\n                       v\n  sys.argv[1] given? --yes--> audio = load_wav_pcm16(wav_path)\n        |no                        (raises w/ ffmpeg fix-it command\n        v                           if format doesn't match)\n  audio = generate_tone_pcm16()\n        |\n        v\n  await manager.initialize_stream()\n        |   (opens REAL bidirectional connection to AWS Bedrock,\n        |    spawns _process_responses() + _process_audio_input())\n        v\n  await manager.send_audio_content_start_event()\n        |   (\"AUDIO content block starting\" -> sent to Bedrock)\n        v\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  chunked send loop  [NEW -- replaces single add_audio_chunk] |\n  |--------------------------------------------------------------|\n  |  chunk_bytes = 100ms worth of 16kHz/16-bit/mono audio        |\n  |  for each 100ms slice of `audio`:                            |\n  |     manager.add_audio_chunk(slice)                           |\n  |        (drops onto audio_input_queue; background loop #1     |\n  |         ships it via send_raw_event() -- same as before)     |\n  |     await asyncio.sleep(0.1)                                 |\n  |        (paces it like a live mic feed instead of one blob)   |\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  await asyncio.sleep(0.5)\n        |   (give the last chunk a moment to actually go out)\n        v\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  event-watch loop   [while True, timeout=8.0]                |\n  |---------------------------------------------------------------\n  |   event = await manager.output_queue.get()                   |\n  |   print(f\"EVENT: {keys}\")                                    |\n  |   \"completionEnd\" in event?  --yes--> break                  |\n  |   8s pass with nothing new?  --------> TimeoutError -> break |\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  drain manager.audio_output_queue --> audio_out bytearray\n        v\n  await manager.close()\n        |   (cancels pending tool tasks + audio_input_task,\n        |    sends audio-end / prompt-end / session-end events,\n        |    closes input_stream, awaits response_task)\n        v\n  +-----------------------------+        +--------------------------------+\n  |  audio_out non-empty?       | yes -->|  write bedrock_test_output.wav |\n  +-----------------------------+        +--------------------------------+\n        | no\n        v\n  print(\"No audio received back.\")\n\nEntry point:  if __name__ == \"__main__\": asyncio.run(main())\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
