      "text": "BedrockStreamManager — Audio In/Out Pipeline",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BedrockStreamManager — Audio In/Out Pipeline",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Gpd-ZDUF0TZVlZ6zfYIW5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 30081.271121759695,
      "y": 3206.663338470366,
      "width": 1861.20068359375,
      "height": 3780,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 682682749,
      "version": 27,
      "versionNonce": 1914786703,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788767282877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "====================== @app.websocket(\"/media-stream\") ======================\n                      (main.py -- bridges Twilio <-> BedrockStreamManager)\n\n  Twilio Media Streams WS  ---receive_text()--->  media_stream(websocket)\n                                                         |\n                                          +--------------+--------------+\n                                          |   while True: branch on     |\n                                          |   msg[\"event\"]              |\n                                          +-----------------------------+\n                                          |            |            |\n                                    \"connected\"     \"start\"      \"media\"        \"stop\"\n                                          |            |            |              |\n                                    just logs          v            v              v\n                                       protocol   (see START below) (see MEDIA)   break loop\n                                                                                   (falls into\n                                                                                    finally:)\n\n  --------------------------- event == \"start\" ---------------------------\n     stream_sid_ref[\"value\"] = streamSid\n     manager = BedrockStreamManager(tool_executor=_tool_executor)\n        |\n        +--> await manager.initialize_stream()          [opens Bedrock session]\n        +--> await manager.send_audio_content_start_event()\n        +--> forward_task = create_task(_forward_nova_audio_to_twilio(...))\n        +--> hangup_task  = create_task(_hangup_after_end_call(...))\n              (both run concurrently with the main receive loop from here on)\n\n  --------------------------- event == \"media\" ----------------------------\n     mulaw_bytes (8kHz, from Twilio)\n        --> mulaw_to_pcm16()        --> pcm16_8k\n        --> resample_pcm16(8k->16k) --> pcm16_16k\n        --> manager.add_audio_chunk(pcm16_16k)\n              (same entry point as test_bedrock_stream.py -- lands on\n               audio_input_queue, drained by _process_audio_input)\n     frame_count += 1\n\n  ------------------- background task: _forward_nova_audio_to_twilio -------------------\n     while True:\n        pcm16_24k = await manager.audio_output_queue.get()\n              (filled by _process_responses' audioOutput branch)\n        --> resample_pcm16(24k->8k)  --> pcm16_8k\n        --> pcm16_to_mulaw()         --> mulaw_out\n        --> slice into 20ms FRAME_BYTES chunks:\n              for each chunk:\n                 websocket.send_text({\"event\":\"media\",\"streamSid\":...,\n                                       \"media\":{\"payload\": base64(chunk)}})\n                 await asyncio.sleep(20ms)\n              (paced deliberately -- sending it all at once overruns\n               Twilio's playback buffer and sounds glitchy)\n     [cancelled from the finally: block]\n\n  --------------------- background task: _hangup_after_end_call ---------------------\n     await manager.call_should_end.wait()\n              (set inside BedrockStreamManager._execute_tool when the\n               model calls endCallTool)\n        |\n        v\n     wait (up to 5s) for audio_output_queue to start filling\n        |\n        v\n     wait for audio_output_queue to fully drain\n        |\n        v\n     sleep(1s) grace period\n        |\n        v\n     await websocket.close()\n              (this makes receive_text() raise WebSocketDisconnect,\n               which is caught below)\n     [cancelled from the finally: block]\n\n  ------------------------------- event == \"stop\" / disconnect -------------------------------\n     \"stop\" event  -----> break out of the while loop\n     WebSocketDisconnect --> caught, logged\n                                    |\n                                    v\n  --------------------------------- finally: ---------------------------------\n     forward_task.cancel()\n     hangup_task.cancel()\n     await manager.close()\n              (full BedrockStreamManager teardown discussed earlier \n               cancels pending tool tasks, sends end events, awaits\n               response_task)\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "====================== @app.websocket(\"/media-stream\") ======================\n                      (main.py -- bridges Twilio <-> BedrockStreamManager)\n\n  Twilio Media Streams WS  ---receive_text()--->  media_stream(websocket)\n                                                         |\n                                          +--------------+--------------+\n                                          |   while True: branch on     |\n                                          |   msg[\"event\"]              |\n                                          +-----------------------------+\n                                          |            |            |\n                                    \"connected\"     \"start\"      \"media\"        \"stop\"\n                                          |            |            |              |\n                                    just logs          v            v              v\n                                       protocol   (see START below) (see MEDIA)   break loop\n                                                                                   (falls into\n                                                                                    finally:)\n\n  --------------------------- event == \"start\" ---------------------------\n     stream_sid_ref[\"value\"] = streamSid\n     manager = BedrockStreamManager(tool_executor=_tool_executor)\n        |\n        +--> await manager.initialize_stream()          [opens Bedrock session]\n        +--> await manager.send_audio_content_start_event()\n        +--> forward_task = create_task(_forward_nova_audio_to_twilio(...))\n        +--> hangup_task  = create_task(_hangup_after_end_call(...))\n              (both run concurrently with the main receive loop from here on)\n\n  --------------------------- event == \"media\" ----------------------------\n     mulaw_bytes (8kHz, from Twilio)\n        --> mulaw_to_pcm16()        --> pcm16_8k\n        --> resample_pcm16(8k->16k) --> pcm16_16k\n        --> manager.add_audio_chunk(pcm16_16k)\n              (same entry point as test_bedrock_stream.py -- lands on\n               audio_input_queue, drained by _process_audio_input)\n     frame_count += 1\n\n  ------------------- background task: _forward_nova_audio_to_twilio -------------------\n     while True:\n        pcm16_24k = await manager.audio_output_queue.get()\n              (filled by _process_responses' audioOutput branch)\n        --> resample_pcm16(24k->8k)  --> pcm16_8k\n        --> pcm16_to_mulaw()         --> mulaw_out\n        --> slice into 20ms FRAME_BYTES chunks:\n              for each chunk:\n                 websocket.send_text({\"event\":\"media\",\"streamSid\":...,\n                                       \"media\":{\"payload\": base64(chunk)}})\n                 await asyncio.sleep(20ms)\n              (paced deliberately -- sending it all at once overruns\n               Twilio's playback buffer and sounds glitchy)\n     [cancelled from the finally: block]\n\n  --------------------- background task: _hangup_after_end_call ---------------------\n     await manager.call_should_end.wait()\n              (set inside BedrockStreamManager._execute_tool when the\n               model calls endCallTool)\n        |\n        v\n     wait (up to 5s) for audio_output_queue to start filling\n        |\n        v\n     wait for audio_output_queue to fully drain\n        |\n        v\n     sleep(1s) grace period\n        |\n        v\n     await websocket.close()\n              (this makes receive_text() raise WebSocketDisconnect,\n               which is caught below)\n     [cancelled from the finally: block]\n\n  ------------------------------- event == \"stop\" / disconnect -------------------------------\n     \"stop\" event  -----> break out of the while loop\n     WebSocketDisconnect --> caught, logged\n                                    |\n                                    v\n  --------------------------------- finally: ---------------------------------\n     forward_task.cancel()\n     hangup_task.cancel()\n     await manager.close()\n              (full BedrockStreamManager teardown discussed earlier \n               cancels pending tool tasks, sends end events, awaits\n               response_task)\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gI8ydM7y8UW9rMXmQ2ck9",
