      "updated": 1787848368323,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "{\n  \"event\": \"start\",\n  \"start\": {\n    \"streamSid\": \"MZxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\",\n    \"callSid\": \"CAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\",\n    ...\n  }\n}\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "{\n  \"event\": \"start\",\n  \"start\": {\n    \"streamSid\": \"MZxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\",\n    \"callSid\": \"CAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\",\n    ...\n  }\n}\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dKlWo1AFfYpOAp0rG1Yfj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 27162.29584229903,
      "y": 3446.6000186073306,
      "width": 1702.798828125,
      "height": 3330,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1776427325,
      "version": 32,
      "versionNonce": 394912723,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787767379017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "=================== _hangup_after_end_call() -- END-OF-CALL TIMING ===================\n\n  await manager.call_should_end.wait()\n        |   (blocks here until endCallTool fires inside BedrockStreamManager)\n        v\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  LOOP 1 -- \"wait for the farewell to BEGIN\"      [BOUNDED, 5s cap]   |\n  |-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  |  deadline = now + END_CALL_MAX_WAIT_FOR_AUDIO_SECONDS (5.0s)         |\n  |                                                                      |\n  |  while audio_output_queue.empty()  AND  time.monotonic() < deadline: |\n  |      sleep(0.1)                                                      |\n  |                                                                      |\n  |  exits via EITHER branch:                                            |\n  |     (a) queue.empty() becomes False                                  |\n  |         --> _process_responses put farewell audio in the queue       |\n  |     (b) deadline passes, queue still empty                           |\n  |         --> Nova never said anything -- safety net, don't hang       |\n  |             forever waiting for audio that's never coming            |\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  LOOP 2 -- \"wait for the farewell to FINISH\"     [UNBOUNDED]         |\n  |-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  |  while not audio_output_queue.empty():                               |\n  |      sleep(0.1)                                                      |\n  |                                                                      |\n  |  keeps polling for as long as _forward_nova_audio_to_twilio is still |\n  |  pulling chunks out of the queue and sending them to Twilio --       |\n  |  no deadline, because we DO want to wait however long it takes       |\n  |  once we know audio is actually flowing (unlike loop 1, where        |\n  |  \"nothing may ever come\" was the case we needed to guard against)    |\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  BLIND SPOT -- queue.empty()==True is not the same as              |\n  |  \"Twilio has actually received every byte\"                         |\n  |---------------------------------------------------------------------\n  |  _forward_nova_audio_to_twilio() may have just done:               |\n  |      chunk = await queue.get()   <-- queue is now empty            |\n  |      for i in range(...):                                          |\n  |          await websocket.send_text(...)                            |\n  |          await asyncio.sleep(20ms)   <-- STILL SENDING, mid-flight |\n  |  Loop 2 already saw \"empty\" and moved on, even though the last     |\n  |  chunk pulled out is still being drip-fed to Twilio 20ms at a time.|\n  +-----------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  await asyncio.sleep(END_CALL_GRACE_PERIOD_SECONDS)   (1.0s)\n        |   <-- exists SPECIFICALLY to cover that blind spot: gives\n        |       whatever's still mid-flight in _forward_nova_audio_to_twilio\n        |       enough time to actually finish sending before we cut the line\n        v\n  await websocket.close()\n\n\n------------------------------- as a timeline -------------------------------\n\n  t=0        call_should_end fires (endCallTool ran)\n             |\n  Loop 1:    |<--- polling every 0.1s, up to 5.0s max --->|\n             |          (stops early the instant queue has audio)\n             |\n  Loop 2:    ...........|<--- polling every 0.1s, NO cap --->|\n                          (stops the instant queue.get() has drained it --\n                           but forward_task may still be mid-frame!)\n                                                              |\n  grace:                                                      |<--1.0s-->|\n                                                                          |\n  close:                                                                  X\n                                                              websocket.close()\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "=================== _hangup_after_end_call() -- END-OF-CALL TIMING ===================\n\n  await manager.call_should_end.wait()\n        |   (blocks here until endCallTool fires inside BedrockStreamManager)\n        v\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  LOOP 1 -- \"wait for the farewell to BEGIN\"      [BOUNDED, 5s cap]   |\n  |-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  |  deadline = now + END_CALL_MAX_WAIT_FOR_AUDIO_SECONDS (5.0s)         |\n  |                                                                      |\n  |  while audio_output_queue.empty()  AND  time.monotonic() < deadline: |\n  |      sleep(0.1)                                                      |\n  |                                                                      |\n  |  exits via EITHER branch:                                            |\n  |     (a) queue.empty() becomes False                                  |\n  |         --> _process_responses put farewell audio in the queue       |\n  |     (b) deadline passes, queue still empty                           |\n  |         --> Nova never said anything -- safety net, don't hang       |\n  |             forever waiting for audio that's never coming            |\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  LOOP 2 -- \"wait for the farewell to FINISH\"     [UNBOUNDED]         |\n  |-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  |  while not audio_output_queue.empty():                               |\n  |      sleep(0.1)                                                      |\n  |                                                                      |\n  |  keeps polling for as long as _forward_nova_audio_to_twilio is still |\n  |  pulling chunks out of the queue and sending them to Twilio --       |\n  |  no deadline, because we DO want to wait however long it takes       |\n  |  once we know audio is actually flowing (unlike loop 1, where        |\n  |  \"nothing may ever come\" was the case we needed to guard against)    |\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  +--------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  BLIND SPOT -- queue.empty()==True is not the same as              |\n  |  \"Twilio has actually received every byte\"                         |\n  |---------------------------------------------------------------------\n  |  _forward_nova_audio_to_twilio() may have just done:               |\n  |      chunk = await queue.get()   <-- queue is now empty            |\n  |      for i in range(...):                                          |\n  |          await websocket.send_text(...)                            |\n  |          await asyncio.sleep(20ms)   <-- STILL SENDING, mid-flight |\n  |  Loop 2 already saw \"empty\" and moved on, even though the last     |\n  |  chunk pulled out is still being drip-fed to Twilio 20ms at a time.|\n  +-----------------------------------------------------------------+\n        |\n        v\n  await asyncio.sleep(END_CALL_GRACE_PERIOD_SECONDS)   (1.0s)\n        |   <-- exists SPECIFICALLY to cover that blind spot: gives\n        |       whatever's still mid-flight in _forward_nova_audio_to_twilio\n        |       enough time to actually finish sending before we cut the line\n        v\n  await websocket.close()\n\n\n------------------------------- as a timeline -------------------------------\n\n  t=0        call_should_end fires (endCallTool ran)\n             |\n  Loop 1:    |<--- polling every 0.1s, up to 5.0s max --->|\n             |          (stops early the instant queue has audio)\n             |\n  Loop 2:    ...........|<--- polling every 0.1s, NO cap --->|\n                          (stops the instant queue.get() has drained it --\n                           but forward_task may still be mid-frame!)\n                                                              |\n  grace:                                                      |<--1.0s-->|\n                                                                          |\n  close:                                                                  X\n                                                              websocket.close()\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
