    },
    {
      "id": "Kq62mrqjTvGBSQ1C95nwC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 26116.30885666439,
      "y": 6350.057404337137,
      "width": 1861.198974609375,
      "height": 2790,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 63684197,
      "version": 7,
      "versionNonce": 1412705131,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788784238107,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CALLER DIALS THE NUMBER\n        │\n        ▼\nTwilio Studio Flow (pre-existing, not ours)\n        │  \"Connect Call To\" widget → transfers the call to an\n        │  external URL (this is the X-Twilio-Service-Flow-Event /\n        │  call_transfer_url header seen on EVERY call in this project)\n        ▼\nPOST /twilio/voice   (voice_gateway, main.py)\n        │  - validates X-Twilio-Signature\n        │  - returns TwiML\n        │\n        │  ═══ CURRENT DIAGNOSTIC BUILD ═══\n        ▼\n   <Response><Play>{PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/greeting.wav</Play></Response>\n        │\n        ▼\nTwilio fetches (or uses a cached copy of) greeting.wav\n        │  - GET /greeting.wav sometimes logged, sometimes not\n        │    (Twilio's own Cache-Control: max-age=259200 header\n        │    suggests it may just replay a cached copy)\n        ▼\n[ audio plays to the caller — UNCONFIRMED whether actually heard ]\n        │\n        ▼\nNo further TwiML verb left\n        │  (this is Twilio's normal, documented behavior — not a bug:\n        │   \"no further verb\" = end the call)\n        ▼\nCall ends automatically  →  POST /twilio/status: completed\n        (~5-8 seconds after /twilio/voice, matching greeting length)\n\n\n── FOR CONTRAST — what a fully-working call is SUPPOSED to look like ──\n\nPOST /twilio/voice\n        ▼\n   <Play>{greeting}</Play><Redirect>{PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/twilio/voice-connect</Redirect>\n        ▼\nTwilio plays greeting, then follows the Redirect\n        ▼\nPOST /twilio/voice-connect\n        ▼\n   <Connect><Stream url=\"wss://.../media-stream\"><Parameter callerNumber /></Stream></Connect>\n        ▼\nGET /media-stream   ← WebSocket upgrade (101 Switching Protocols)\n        │\n        ▼\nBedrockStreamManager  ⇄  Nova Sonic (live conversation)\n        │\n        ▼\nendCallTool → farewell → hangup\n\n\n── WHERE IT'S BREAKING ──\n\nConfirmed working:        <Say>...</Say>                → audible ✅\nConfirmed broken (x2):    <Play>+<Connect><Stream>       → never reaches media-stream ❌\nConfirmed broken (x1):    <Play>+<Redirect>→<Connect>     → voice-connect fetched, still\n                                                             never reaches media-stream ❌\nStill unconfirmed:        <Play> alone                    → waiting on your ear, not logs\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CALLER DIALS THE NUMBER\n        │\n        ▼\nTwilio Studio Flow (pre-existing, not ours)\n        │  \"Connect Call To\" widget → transfers the call to an\n        │  external URL (this is the X-Twilio-Service-Flow-Event /\n        │  call_transfer_url header seen on EVERY call in this project)\n        ▼\nPOST /twilio/voice   (voice_gateway, main.py)\n        │  - validates X-Twilio-Signature\n        │  - returns TwiML\n        │\n        │  ═══ CURRENT DIAGNOSTIC BUILD ═══\n        ▼\n   <Response><Play>{PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/greeting.wav</Play></Response>\n        │\n        ▼\nTwilio fetches (or uses a cached copy of) greeting.wav\n        │  - GET /greeting.wav sometimes logged, sometimes not\n        │    (Twilio's own Cache-Control: max-age=259200 header\n        │    suggests it may just replay a cached copy)\n        ▼\n[ audio plays to the caller — UNCONFIRMED whether actually heard ]\n        │\n        ▼\nNo further TwiML verb left\n        │  (this is Twilio's normal, documented behavior — not a bug:\n        │   \"no further verb\" = end the call)\n        ▼\nCall ends automatically  →  POST /twilio/status: completed\n        (~5-8 seconds after /twilio/voice, matching greeting length)\n\n\n── FOR CONTRAST — what a fully-working call is SUPPOSED to look like ──\n\nPOST /twilio/voice\n        ▼\n   <Play>{greeting}</Play><Redirect>{PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/twilio/voice-connect</Redirect>\n        ▼\nTwilio plays greeting, then follows the Redirect\n        ▼\nPOST /twilio/voice-connect\n        ▼\n   <Connect><Stream url=\"wss://.../media-stream\"><Parameter callerNumber /></Stream></Connect>\n        ▼\nGET /media-stream   ← WebSocket upgrade (101 Switching Protocols)\n        │\n        ▼\nBedrockStreamManager  ⇄  Nova Sonic (live conversation)\n        │\n        ▼\nendCallTool → farewell → hangup\n\n\n── WHERE IT'S BREAKING ──\n\nConfirmed working:        <Say>...</Say>                → audible ✅\nConfirmed broken (x2):    <Play>+<Connect><Stream>       → never reaches media-stream ❌\nConfirmed broken (x1):    <Play>+<Redirect>→<Connect>     → voice-connect fetched, still\n                                                             never reaches media-stream ❌\nStill unconfirmed:        <Play> alone                    → waiting on your ear, not logs\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
